// profilePurgeRegistry is the compiled, fixed physical purge plan executed by the
// shared phasedpurge.Turn engine (P2-62 / O022). Every table, column, predicate,
// guard and key is a source constant: no identifier, column or ordering decision
// ever comes from a job row, a request or a database reflection at run time.
//
// Phase numbers are connected components of the blocking foreign-key graph, not
// elapsed stages. The engine rewinds a blocked parent to the first unit of the
// same phase, so a child drain and every parent it can block must share one
// phase; splitting them would leave a child outside the window unreachable.
//
// Guards are emitted for every blocking foreign-key child of a parent table,
// including children whose own unit drains through a different parent. The
// candidate row is chosen first in a MATERIALIZED window and only that row is
// checked against its children, so reads stay constant however many parents are
// still waiting.
//
// Destructive units seek the lowest remaining indexed head and pass no cursor:
// removing or scrubbing the row removes it from the pending predicate.
// Session-token children retain their token mapper until all children drain;
// no private child loses the ownership path required to resume cleanup.
//
// readBound is the compiled per-turn read proof: the candidate and its key seek,
// 32 per parent hop (returned rows plus empty index probes), one per owned-child guard, and the declared worst case of
// every AFTER DELETE/UPDATE trigger body (one read per DML statement and per
// subquery SELECT). The engine refuses a plan that cannot fit owner 12 + unit 116.
